## Why This Is Asked

This question probes on-device real-time hazard detection and 3D distance estimation under unseen categories, reflecting safety-critical constraints common in field deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth on edge
- On-device meta-learning (5-shot)
- Synthetic+real data with domain randomization
- Temporal tracking and occlusion robustness
- Evaluation: detection, depth error, latency

## Code Example

```javascript
function forward(img, backbone, detectorHead, depthHead) {
  const feats = backbone.extract(img);
  const boxes = detectorHead.predict(feats);
  const depth = depthHead.predict(feats);
  return { boxes, depth };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ablate depth head accuracy vs. detector latency?
- What failure modes dominate in cluttered sites, and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses capability to design edge-friendly 3D pose systems for dynamic outdoor scenes, handling wind-induced blur, occlusion, and rapid adaptation to new bolt geometries with minimal on-device training.

## Key Concepts

- Edge latency and memory constraints on embedded GPUs
- Monocular 3D pose estimation (6-DoF) from moving cameras
- Few-shot on-device adaptation (2-shot)
- Synthetic-to-real transfer with domain randomization
- Robustness to motion blur and lighting variation

## Code Example

```javascript
function fineTuneAdapter(model, supportImages, supportLabels) {
  // tiny adapter fine-tune on-device
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    const batch = getBatch(supportImages, supportLabels);
    const loss = model.computeLoss(batch);
    model.backward(loss);
  }
  return model;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure generalization to new turbine models or bolt types?
- What guardrails prevent false positives in flight-critical decisions?
